  {
   "t": "note",
   "kind": "warn",
   "x": "The letter *y* is `KWR*` when glued but `KWH` in the modifier dictionary and in [spelling mode](#/ref/spelling-mode). Every other letter has the same chord in all three."
  },
  {
   "t": "note",
   "kind": "warn",
   "x": "`LGTS` strokes with a vowel-only chord have no hyphen: `A`, `E`, `U`, `EU` are written `AFLGTS`, `EFLGTS`, `UFLGTS`, `EUFLGTS`. Chords ending in a consonant key need the hyphen: `S-FLGTS`, `KR-FLGTS`."
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "x": "Fingerspelling in running text"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "x": "To spell a word in the text, strike the letter's chord with the star. The star glues it to the letters beside it and to nothing else. Add `-P` for a capital."
  },
  {
   "t": "table",
   "head": [
    "Stroke",
    "Writes",
    "Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "a letter chord plus `*`",
     "that letter, lowercase",
     "[[A*]] [[PW*]] [[KR*]] [[TK*]] [[*E]] write a b c d e"
    ],
    [
     "the same plus `-P`",
     "that letter, capitalized",
     "[[A*P]] [[PW*P]] [[KR*P]] write A B C"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "x": "Letters glue to each other: [[KR*P]] [[A*]] [[T*]] writes ` Cat` as one word (the first letter starts a new word, so the space comes before it)."
  },
  {
   "t": "note",
   "kind": "rule",
   "x": "The 52 strokes (26 lowercase, 26 capital) are reserved ahead of every word, so a word that wanted one moves to its next-cheapest outline: [[captain|KAPT]] instead of `K*P`, [[eh|A*EU]] instead of `*E`."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "x": "Not ported from Plover: the number-bar chords, the `-RBGS` forms, and the trailing-hyphen or trailing-period forms."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "x": "A word with no outline of its own (see [briefs](#/ref/briefs)) is costed by the generator as exactly this: one stroke per letter."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "x": "There is no physical key for [spelling mode](#/ref/spelling-mode) yet, so glued letters are how you spell a word out today."
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "x": "Modifier chords: the LGTS dictionary"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "x": "Every lookup this dictionary answers is written as:"
  },
  {
   "t": "pre",
   "x": "[chord for the key] + [modifier keys on the right hand] + LGTS"
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "items": [
    "The ender `LGTS` (the right hand's bottom four keys, `-LGTS`) is on every one of the 5,475 strokes. It exists only so that an ordinary word's outline never collides with a modifier chord.",
    "At least one modifier key must be held. A bare letter or symbol with no modifier is not this dictionary's job.",
    "The output is wrapped in `{^}` on both sides, so it attaches to nothing and adds no space."
   ],
   "ordered": false
  },
